<title>GERMANY: Krupp says mark uncertainty hurting investment.</title>
<headline>Krupp says mark uncertainty hurting investment.</headline>
<dateline>KIEL, Germany 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bundesbank council member Hans-Juergen Krupp said on Tuesday that investment in Germany was being hampered by uncertainty over the mark exchange rate.</p>
<p>&quot;Investment in Germany today has become a gamble,&quot; Krupp told a panel discussion. He added that sharp swings in the mark exchange rate had put exporters under great pressure.</p>
<p>But commenting on what he said was &quot;panic fostering&quot; relating to the introduction of the planned European single currency, Krupp warned that investment in the dollar also entailed risks, given the fact that it had &quot;moved up and down&quot; in recent years.</p>
<p>Krupp was speaking at a seminar held by the DAG union.</p>
<p>-- David Crossland, Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
